  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1217 AM CST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\nThe long term portion of the forecast remains quiet as our area \nremains just south of the active storm track across the central \nCONUS. There is the chance that any storm systems dig further south \nand clip our area but for now models have our area dry That being \nsaid we should see a nice warmup in temps both highs and lows \nstarting as early as Friday with highs reaching into the mid 60s. \nThe weekend looks even better as highs ramp up back into the 70s \nboth days as return southerly flow returns. Lows during this period \nwill range from the 40s Saturday morning to the 50s Sunday morning \nbefore settling back down into the 40s Monday morning as another \nshot of colder air works its way southward out ahead of yet another \ndry cold front across the area overnight. Highs behind this front \nlook to drop back into the 60s before ramping up back into the 70 \nmiddle of next week.",
